{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"galloping-duncical-groundhog","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\n\n`reconcile-check` still packages several distinct observables together: field-diff discrepancies, orphaned bindings, unbound counts, summary tallies, text formatting, exit behavior, and the persisted report. The legacy follow-on removals in 82bb and c195 both depend on first proving which of those observations belong to `bridge preview`, `bridge fsck`, `bridge status`, or a narrowly-scoped new bridge diagnostic surface.\n\n## Approach\n\nCharacterize the current `reconcile-check` outputs, assign each observable to its canonical bridge owner, and implement the bridge-side routing or any one new diagnostic subverb required to preserve the useful surface. Migrate persisted report construction away from `bridge_state/reconcile-check.json` only insofar as this observable-to-owner move requires it, and record explicit retirement evidence for any field that does not survive the migration.\n\n## Scope\n\n- direct reconcile-check report construction and output shaping in `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler`\n- canonical `bridge preview` / `bridge fsck` / `bridge status` CLI result contracts in `src/rebar/_cli`\n- bridge diagnostics surfaced through library/MCP shims only where needed to preserve the canonical bridge result contract before c195 removes compatibility entrypoints\n- migration docs and characterization tests covering healthy, discrepant, orphaned, and unbound cases\n\n## Testing\n\nAdd RED-first characterization coverage that captures current healthy, discrepant, orphaned, and unbound observations; then prove the canonical bridge owners expose the preserved diagnostics, formatting, exits, and persisted-report behavior or an explicit retirement.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Every current reconcile-check observable is assigned to `bridge preview`, `bridge fsck`, `bridge status`, or an explicit approved retirement.\n- [ ] Preview exposes field-diff discrepancies, fsck exposes binding/integrity diagnostics, and status exposes operational witnesses with stable names.\n- [ ] Any newly introduced bridge diagnostic subverb has one coherent responsibility and a stable result contract.\n- [ ] Persisted report behavior is migrated away from `bridge_state/reconcile-check.json` with field/format/exit parity or explicit retirement evidence.\n- [ ] Characterization and canonical bridge tests cover healthy, discrepant, orphaned, and unbound cases.","id":"bec7-d2ff-79d0-40ff","parent_id":"3b66-615c-fbfb-4b1f","priority":1,"tags":["janitor","reconciler","bridge","migration"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Canonicalize reconcile-check diagnostics"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788425626666764001,"uuid":"8389419b-08a6-4b53-911d-54a3af542d5c"}